      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are hundreds of different types of birthday cakes in the world. You probably ate one on your last birthday. But have you ever wondered: Why am I eating this on my birthday?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Ancient Egyptians were said to have invented the celebration of birthdays. They believed that when "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pharaohs",
            "zh": "法老"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "crowned",
            "ref": "v-crown"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", they became gods. So their "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "coronation",
            "zh": "加冕"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " day was their “birthday” as a god. There would be many activities to celebrate this great day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Ancient Greeks borrowed this tradition from the Egyptians. Then they thought that a dessert would make the celebration more meaningful. So they baked moon-shaped cakes to offer to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Artemis",
            "zh": "阿尔忒弥斯"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", goddess of the moon, as a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "tribute",
            "ref": "v-tribute"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They decorated the cakes with candles to make them shine like the moon."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Modern birthday parties are said to have their roots in an 18th-century German celebration. On the morning of a child’s birthday, he or she would receive a cake with lighted candles. The candles "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "added up to",
            "ref": "v-add-up-to"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the kid’s age, plus one. This extra candle was called the “light of life”. It "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "represented",
            "ref": "v-represent"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the hope that another full year would be lived."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
